content.text:
verdict: findings
scenario_results:
  - {scenario: 1 (decidable without annex), result: fail, notes: "Ask 1's amendment cannot be pinned down from the brief (says five sections, lists six); ask 2's actual content to approve lives only in annex §4 and the three roles are never named."}
  - {scenario: 2 (first paragraph answers), result: pass, notes: "Paragraph 1 states it: 'Recommendation: enrich the role-definition typedef with five sections... re-author the three roles... import the skill catalogue by kind.'"}
  - {scenario: 3 (no unintroduced terms), result: fail, notes: "Non-empty list: 'keeper sources', 'intent-provenance carrier', 'demand-pulled', 'session skills'; SFIA and RAPID/DACI get only the collective framing 'external practice', no gloss."}
  - {scenario: 4 (asks complete, gating stated), result: fail, notes: "Gating sentence present ('Asks 1–3 gate the work; ask 4 defaults on silence') but ask 3 read in isolation carries no evidence, only annex pointers, and ask 2's evidence is a single parenthetical claim."}
ask_decidability: ["ask 1: wobbly — the text says 'Add five sections' then lists six (Default posture, Decision rights, Admissible evidence, Interfaces, Knowledge and skills, Anti-rationalization); I cannot tell which set I would be approving", "ask 2: wobbly — the three roles are never individually named, the per-role content is annex-only, and 'keeper sources' is undefined; I can approve the sequencing but not what the roles will say", "ask 3: wobbly — the by-kind dispositions and counts are clear, but 'intent-provenance carrier' and 'demand-pulled' are unexplained and no inline evidence says why this split is right", "ask 4: confident — the grant, the resulting typedef rule, and the default ('rides ask 3') are all stated inline"]
overload: "right-sized for one reading — four asks, evidence summarized inline, annex correctly labeled optional; the density problem is coinage, not length"
stumbles: ["Add five sections: Default posture, Decision rights (decides + escalates), Admissible evidence, Interfaces, Knowledge and skills, Anti-rationalization — that is six items after the word 'five', and the opening paragraph also promised five", "old templates as keeper sources — 'keeper sources' arrives cold; I cannot tell if it means source-of-truth, reference-only, or something else", "typed terminal artifacts (the intent-provenance carrier) — the parenthetical is itself an unexplained coinage, so it glosses nothing", "~950 lines of incident patches across the two old templates — the two templates are never identified, so the central evidence claim rests on unnamed documents", "~19 technique skills imported ... demand-pulled — 'demand-pulled' is coined mid-ask without a gloss"]
unintroduced_terms: ["keeper sources", "intent-provenance carrier", "demand-pulled / demand-pull", "session skills (category used before any definition)", "SFIA (no gloss; least guessable of the external names)", "RAPID/DACI (framed only as 'external practice')", "the two old templates (referenced, never named)"]
top_changes: ["Fix the five/six mismatch in ask 1: state the true count and make the list match it in both the opening paragraph and the ask — as written the amendment being approved is ambiguous", "Make each ask self-sufficient per the rubric: add one inline evidence clause to asks 2 and 3 (ask 3 currently has only annex pointers), and name the three roles in ask 2", "Gloss or drop the coinages at first use — 'keeper sources', 'intent-provenance carrier', 'demand-pulled' — and give SFIA/RAPID-DACI a five-word gloss each"]
